  "answer": "I found no earlier ticket asking for this exact feature: an opt-in, consent-gated automation surface that covers session listing, buffer reads and input. Two older tickets are related. terminal#9368 asked for a `wt send-input` subcommand. In April 2026 it was moved to rejected because of the security risk of letting other processes inject input, especially now that mixed elevation exists. In that thread [user] also said that a setting stored only in settings.json wouldn't stop malicious.exe from editing it. terminal#4472 is the older general backlog item for remote control of a running terminal instance, and it mentions a possible `list-sessions` command. Neither covers reading buffers or an authenticated opt-in model. Keep this as a separate feature request. In it, explain how the design answers the objections in #9368: consent stored outside settings.json, a hard exclusion of elevated windows, and read access separate from input. Until something like this exists, `wt` can only create and focus tabs and panes. The only workaround for injecting input is the `sendInput` action bound to a key in your own settings."
 },
